window.CET6_DATA("data/articles/day-075.json",{"day":75,"title":"What a Library Teaches Beyond Books","targetWords":[{"word":"college","gloss":"大学","context":"On her first morning at college, Mei expected the library to provide a quiet seat and a textbook.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"example","gloss":"例子","context":"A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"class","gloss":"班级","context":"Instead, a librarian asked her to bring a real question from her class.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"course","gloss":"课程","context":"By the end of the course, Mei understood why a campus needed more than impressive buildings.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"term","gloss":"学期","context":"A single grade could not capture everything the pupil had learned during a term.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"paper","gloss":"论文","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"subject","gloss":"主题","context":"The subject was public health, and her task was to write an essay on unequal access to care.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"list","gloss":"清单","context":"For the next lecture, Mei built a list of sources rather than simply collecting quotations.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"task","gloss":"任务","context":"The subject was public health, and her task was to write an essay on unequal access to care.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"type","gloss":"类型","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"essay","gloss":"论文","context":"The subject was public health, and her task was to write an essay on unequal access to care.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"graduate","gloss":"研究生的","context":"A graduate mentor described the library as a place where every answer could become another lesson.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"lecture","gloss":"讲课","context":"For the next lecture, Mei built a list of sources rather than simply collecting quotations.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"model","gloss":"模型","context":"A scholar from a local institute helped her distinguish a useful model from a prediction that exceeded the data.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"grade","gloss":"分数","context":"A single grade could not capture everything the pupil had learned during a term.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"newspaper","gloss":"报纸","context":"A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"phrase","gloss":"短语","context":"A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"method","gloss":"方法","context":"The method was modest: observe carefully, try one change, and review the result.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"article","gloss":"文章","context":"A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"intellectual","gloss":"知识的","context":"The librarian suggested that an intellectual discipline begins when an attractive claim becomes a question that can be investigated.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"title","gloss":"标题","context":"The title on a document was no guarantee of reliability, and a page full of technical vocabulary could conceal weak reasoning as easily as it could explain strong evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"textbook","gloss":"课本","context":"On her first morning at college, Mei expected the library to provide a quiet seat and a textbook.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"magazine","gloss":"杂志","context":"A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"library","gloss":"图书馆","context":"On her first morning at college, Mei expected the library to provide a quiet seat and a textbook.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"journal","gloss":"期刊","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"lesson","gloss":"课","context":"A graduate mentor described the library as a place where every answer could become another lesson.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"campus","gloss":"校园","context":"By the end of the course, Mei understood why a campus needed more than impressive buildings.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"classroom","gloss":"教室","context":"She kept a file of questions that arose in the classroom and asked a faculty adviser for guidance.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"vocabulary","gloss":"词汇","context":"The title on a document was no guarantee of reliability, and a page full of technical vocabulary could conceal weak reasoning as easily as it could explain strong evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"page","gloss":"页码","context":"The title on a document was no guarantee of reliability, and a page full of technical vocabulary could conceal weak reasoning as easily as it could explain strong evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"discipline","gloss":"学科","context":"The librarian suggested that an intellectual discipline begins when an attractive claim becomes a question that can be investigated.","contextParagraph":0,"collocation":null},{"word":"sample","gloss":"样本","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"pupil","gloss":"学生","context":"As an undergraduate volunteer, she helped an elementary school pupil with homework.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"grammar","gloss":"语法","context":"The principal had asked volunteers to follow the curriculum, but Mei found that a grammar exercise became more meaningful when linked to a story the child wanted to tell.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"homework","gloss":"作业","context":"As an undergraduate volunteer, she helped an elementary school pupil with homework.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"institute","gloss":"机构","context":"A scholar from a local institute helped her distinguish a useful model from a prediction that exceeded the data.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"scholar","gloss":"学者","context":"A scholar from a local institute helped her distinguish a useful model from a prediction that exceeded the data.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"chapter","gloss":"章节","context":"An excerpt from an older chapter showed that the debate had a history.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"faculty","gloss":"教师","context":"She kept a file of questions that arose in the classroom and asked a faculty adviser for guidance.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"undergraduate","gloss":"本科生","context":"As an undergraduate volunteer, she helped an elementary school pupil with homework.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"document","gloss":"文档","context":"The title on a document was no guarantee of reliability, and a page full of technical vocabulary could conceal weak reasoning as easily as it could explain strong evidence.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"procedure","gloss":"步骤","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"excerpt","gloss":"摘录","context":"An excerpt from an older chapter showed that the debate had a history.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"curriculum","gloss":"课程","context":"The principal had asked volunteers to follow the curriculum, but Mei found that a grammar exercise became more meaningful when linked to a story the child wanted to tell.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"license","gloss":"许可","context":"Tuition paid for access to people, resources, and opportunities to revise mistakes, not a license to stop questioning.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"tuition","gloss":"学费","context":"Tuition paid for access to people, resources, and opportunities to revise mistakes, not a license to stop questioning.","contextParagraph":3,"collocation":null},{"word":"laboratory","gloss":"实验室","context":"She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results.","contextParagraph":1,"collocation":null},{"word":"elementary","gloss":"小学的","context":"As an undergraduate volunteer, she helped an elementary school pupil with homework.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"file","gloss":"档案","context":"She kept a file of questions that arose in the classroom and asked a faculty adviser for guidance.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null},{"word":"principal","gloss":"校长","context":"The principal had asked volunteers to follow the curriculum, but Mei found that a grammar exercise became more meaningful when linked to a story the child wanted to tell.","contextParagraph":2,"collocation":null}],"paragraphs":[{"en":"On her first morning at college, Mei expected the library to provide a quiet seat and a textbook. Instead, a librarian asked her to bring a real question from her class. The subject was public health, and her task was to write an essay on unequal access to care. A newspaper article offered a vivid example, while a magazine supplied a memorable phrase. Neither explained how the evidence had been collected. The librarian suggested that an intellectual discipline begins when an attractive claim becomes a question that can be investigated.","zh":"大学第一天早晨，梅以为图书馆只会提供一个安静座位和一本教材。馆员却请她带来课堂上的真实问题。课程主题是公共健康，她的任务是写一篇关于医疗服务机会不平等的论文。报纸文章提供了生动例子，杂志提供了一句令人印象深刻的话，但两者都没有解释证据如何收集。馆员认为，一门知识学科的起点，是把吸引人的主张转化为可以调查的问题。"},{"en":"For the next lecture, Mei built a list of sources rather than simply collecting quotations. She compared a journal paper with a laboratory report, checked the type of sample each used, and recorded the procedure behind the results. A scholar from a local institute helped her distinguish a useful model from a prediction that exceeded the data. An excerpt from an older chapter showed that the debate had a history. The title on a document was no guarantee of reliability, and a page full of technical vocabulary could conceal weak reasoning as easily as it could explain strong evidence.","zh":"准备下一次讲课时，梅列出资料清单，而不是简单收集引文。她比较期刊论文和实验室报告，检查各自使用的样本类型，并记录得出结果的研究程序。当地研究所的学者帮助她区分有用的模型和超出数据支持范围的预测。旧书一章的节选表明，这场争论有其历史。文献的标题无法保证可靠性；满页技术词汇既可能解释有力证据，也可能掩盖薄弱推理。"},{"en":"These lessons also changed her work outside the library. As an undergraduate volunteer, she helped an elementary school pupil with homework. The principal had asked volunteers to follow the curriculum, but Mei found that a grammar exercise became more meaningful when linked to a story the child wanted to tell. She kept a file of questions that arose in the classroom and asked a faculty adviser for guidance. The method was modest: observe carefully, try one change, and review the result. A single grade could not capture everything the pupil had learned during a term.","zh":"这些经验也改变了她在图书馆之外的工作。作为本科生志愿者，她辅导一位小学生完成作业。校长要求志愿者遵照课程设置，但梅发现，当语法练习与孩子想讲述的故事相联系时，练习更有意义。她把课堂中出现的问题存档，并向教师顾问请教。这种方法很朴素：认真观察，尝试一项改变，再审视结果。一个学期里的单次分数无法反映学生学到的一切。"},{"en":"By the end of the course, Mei understood why a campus needed more than impressive buildings. Tuition paid for access to people, resources, and opportunities to revise mistakes, not a license to stop questioning. A graduate mentor described the library as a place where every answer could become another lesson. Mei's final essay retained its concern for unequal care, but its argument was clearer and its evidence more cautious. What had begun as a search for a book became an education in responsibility: making claims that others could examine, and being willing to improve them when the evidence demanded it.","zh":"课程结束时，梅明白了大学校园为何需要的不仅是气派建筑。学费换来的是接触人员、资源和纠正错误的机会，而不是停止质疑的许可。一位研究生导师把图书馆形容为一个地方：每个答案都可能成为下一课。梅的最终论文仍关心医疗机会不平等，但论证更加清晰，对证据的使用更加谨慎。最初寻找一本书的行动，最终成为责任教育：提出别人能够检验的主张，并愿意在证据要求时改进它们。"},{"en":"When a friend later asked where to find a quick answer, Mei still offered practical help. She did not believe every everyday question required a research project. But she had learned to recognize situations in which a convenient answer could cause harm: a medical decision, an accusation, or a claim about an unfamiliar community. In those cases, checking a source was not an unnecessary academic ritual. It was a small act of care for the people affected by the conclusion. The library had taught her how to pause before turning information into authority.","zh":"后来朋友问哪里能迅速找到答案，梅仍提供实用帮助。她不认为每个日常问题都需要研究项目，但学会识别便捷答案可能造成伤害的情况：医疗决定、指控，或针对陌生群体的主张。在这些情况下，核查来源不是多余学术仪式，而是关心会受到结论影响的人。图书馆教会她在把信息变成权威之前停一停。"}],"previous":74,"next":76});
